  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\alpha, \\beta$ be the distinct roots of the equation $x^2-\\left(t^2-5 t+6\\right) x+1=0, t \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and $a_n=\\alpha^n+\\beta^n$. Then the minimum value of $\\frac{a_{2023}+a_{2025}}{a_{2024}}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$-1 / 4$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-1 / 4$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$-1 / 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1 / 4$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "by newton's theorem\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}+2}-\\left(\\mathrm{t}^2-5 \\mathrm{t}+6\\right) \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}+1}+\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}}=0 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{a}_{2025}+\\mathrm{a}_{2023}=\\left(\\mathrm{t}^2-5 \\mathrm{t}+6\\right) \\mathrm{a}_{2024} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{a}_{2025}+\\mathrm{a}_{2023}}{\\mathrm{a}_{2024}}=\\mathrm{t}^2-5 \\mathrm{t}+6 \\\\\n& \\because \\mathrm{t}^2-5 \\mathrm{t}+6=\\left(\\mathrm{t}-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\text { minimum value }=-\\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}